/** Brand marks for the Technical Arsenal.
 *
 *  Most come from devicon v2.16.0 (MIT) in their `-original` form, which keeps
 *  each logo's real colours: Docker's nine blues, GitLab's three-tone fox,
 *  Python's and Node's gradients. Nine have no multi-colour version anywhere,
 *  so those are Simple Icons' single-colour silhouettes in the brand's own hex.
 *
 *  Each viewBox is cropped to the artwork's measured bounding box, so a logo
 *  fills its slot instead of floating inside the source file's padding. Wide
 *  marks (AWS, Docker, Tailwind) therefore render wider than tall, which is why
 *  the chip sizes them by height.
 *
 *  Gradient ids are prefixed with the slug. devicon names several of them "a"
 *  and "b", and since every mark is inlined into one document, Node.js was
 *  painting itself with Next.js's gradients before they were namespaced.
 *
 *  Entries that are practices rather than products (RAG, LLM Evals, Prompt &
 *  Context Engineering) have no mark and fall back to a lucide glyph. */

type Mark = { viewBox: string; inner: string };

